# Copy this file to ".env" for LOCAL backend development. The .env file is
# gitignored — never commit real tokens.
#
# FRONTEND: there are NO secret frontend variables. Any VITE_ variable is
# bundled into the public client code by Vite, so API keys must never use the
# VITE_ prefix. The only frontend variable is:
#
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL   (optional) point the traffic/air/cpcb/waqi clients at a
#                      non-same-origin backend for local dev
#
# SERVER-ONLY API KEYS — set these in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables
# (or your local backend environment), NOT in frontend code:
#
#   TOMTOM_API_KEY     live TomTom traffic ETAs
#   OPENAQ_API_KEY     OpenAQ ground sensors (primary CPCB air source)
#   DATAGOV_KEY        data.gov.in resource API (legacy CPCB fallback)
#   WAQI_TOKEN         WAQI nearest-station lookup (aqicn.org/data-platform/token/)
#
# ROTATION NOTE: a shared data.gov.in sample API key was previously committed
# to this repo (src and .env.example) and baked into public builds. Treat it
# as burned: generate your own key at https://data.gov.in and never commit it.
